## Approved diagnosis (supervisor)
- Owner layer: framework error model (`00-foundation/07-framework-error-model.ko.md:75-85`) and routing
  (`03-spot-actor/08-routing.ko.md:322-331`): a route that was never admitted / lost = `Unavailable`; only an actual reply
  deadline expiry = `DeadlineExceeded`. Sender replay policy: `03-spot-actor/04-actor-model.ko.md` (new bullets after
  "Terminal record가 original deadline 뒤 5분…"): retry within the whole remaining deadline, end with DeadlineExceeded only
  when the deadline itself is exhausted while an admitted request is outstanding.
- Defect: `raw_mesh_node_owner.cpp:230-235` retries initial `route_unavailable`; when the deadline runs out during that
  pre-admission retry, `request_bound_session_bind()` (`raw_mesh_node_owner.cpp:1922-1939`) designates
  `operation_terminal_t::timed_out`, and `mesh_node_runtime.cpp:3850-3857` cannot tell "retry exhausted, never admitted"
  from "admitted, reply timed out", so it maps both to `DeadlineExceeded`. Restored m6b assertion
  (`test_cpp_framework_m6b_runtime.cpp:1320`) fails on this. Class B (pre-existing defect, exposed once the ENOENT merge
  was undone).

## What to do
1. Carry the terminal kind through: the raw owner reports a distinct terminal (e.g. `route_unavailable` exhausted vs
   `timed_out` after admission) — one owner of that decision (the raw owner knows whether any attempt was admitted). The
   mesh runtime maps exhausted-before-admission → `Unavailable`, admitted-then-no-reply → `DeadlineExceeded`. No second
   classification table; reuse the adapter's structured result from stage 1.
2. Cross-language parity (report, do not edit): how dotnet (`ZLinkSubmitFailureMapper` / actor join terminal), java and
   node map "never admitted within the deadline" — same kind? If a language differs, list it as a follow-up.
3. Regression: the restored m6b case + a focused unit test in `test_cpp_framework_m6b_runtime.cpp` or the execution tests
   that drives both terminals (route absent for the whole deadline → Unavailable; admitted, reply withheld → DeadlineExceeded).
4. Verify: the four unit binaries + `ctest -R 'm6a|m6b|channel_messaging|execution|raw_route_port'`; then the full
   `ctest --test-dir ... -j2` once (known C: inventory 278).

